  "elderLines": [
    {
      "id": "maren_tam",
      "hunted": "tidecaller",
      "lines": [
        "Tam's ladle. Gods. He cooked for us all the way up - stew on a mountain, in the snow.",
        "He said a hero who eats well fights well. He was the first to laugh and the first to stand when it went wrong.",
        "Wenna's brother. I should have gone down to Saltmere years ago and told her. I'll go. When this is done, I'll go."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "maren_ingot",
      "hunted": "seam_warden",
      "lines": [
        "Black iron with our five marks on it. We dug the seal's iron at Blackiron ourselves.",
        "Oskar swung the pick, Liane did the sums, Tam fed the miners and Morvax paid. I set my mark last.",
        "I was so proud of that mark. Look at it. Still there."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "maren_oskar",
      "hunted": "hollow_captain",
      "lines": [
        "Oskar's shield. He left it at Greyhold and told his captain to keep it till he came home.",
        "He carried Liane the last mile up and complained the whole way. And Hale kept it fifty years?",
        "...Of course he did. That was Greyhold."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "maren_liane",
      "hunted": "rimefang",
      "lines": [
        "Her lantern. Liane lit it the night before we climbed and said she'd blow it out herself when we were all home.",
        "She wrote everything down, you know. Every day of it.",
        "And Aske kept her door fifty years. ...She'd have told him off for it, and been pleased."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "maren_confession",
      "lines": [
        "Sit. No, sit. I've been fifty years getting this wrong in my head, and now I'll get it wrong out loud.",
        "It wasn't a rockfall. Morvax wanted the kings' gold, to make Pixelheim a city fit for us. Fafnyr was half awake, so Morvax promised him his freedom for the hoard.",
        "A lie, and the dragon knew it. The hall came down. Tam and Oskar and Liane held up the roof so I could get out. I made up the rockfall on the way home. It sounded tidier.",
        "Some nights I saw a lamp up there. I told myself it was a star. I was too proud to climb, and so was he. Two old fools and a mountain.",
        "(She takes a letter from her sleeve, and the brooch with five marks on it, hers the last.) My promise, courier: the fifth mark. And this. It has an address now."
      ]
    }
  ],
